      "## Research question and scope",
      "This protocol asks how long it takes to fill an unplanned absence from the moment the absence is known to the moment a qualified replacement is confirmed. The unit is one uncovered shift or shift segment, not one message or one candidate contact. The study measures elapsed time and the reasons for delay. It does not claim that a faster fill is always better if the replacement is unqualified or the schedule becomes unsafe.",
      "Set the scope to one site, one client, or one type of role and record the coverage rules, the approval path. The systems used for availability. If the team changes its fallback or overtime policy during the window, keep the earlier definition for the whole sample or split the period. A fill that is fast because a rule was bypassed is a different event from a fill that followed the approved path.",
