      "Compare cases within the same stratum and inspect the slowest tail. A site with a stable median and a few very old cases has a different problem from a site with uniformly slow fills. Present the reasons for delay as categories with counts, and quote a short case description only when it helps explain a pattern. Avoid ranking individual supervisors by fill time.",
      "## Limitations and sources of error",
      "The absence export may not capture informal coverage, early notice, or shifts that were canceled before a replacement was needed. A fast fill can reflect a loose approval process rather than good planning, and a slow fill can reflect appropriate caution. The protocol measures elapsed time and recorded states, not service quality or worker welfare. Local leave rules and contractual requirements need separate review.",
      "Small samples limit precision, especially when the site has few credentialed roles. A change in client demand during the window can affect both the number of absences and the willingness to approve overtime. Record those conditions and avoid presenting the result as a universal benchmark. If the data cannot support a rate, report counts and describe the cases instead.",
